</span></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S0.T1.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Extended Data Table 1</span>: </span><span id="S0.T1.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
<span id="S0.T1.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Dataset statistics for text-to-image training pipeline.</span> Our training process consists of two stages: <span id="S0.T1.8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Stage I (Vision-Language Pretraining)</span> utilizes the OpenChest dataset (approximately 960K image-text pairs) for foundation pretraining, where GPT-4 converts medical metadata from multiple public datasets into standardized radiological descriptions. <span id="S0.T1.8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Stage II (Vision-Language Alignment)</span> employs clinical reports from the MIMIC-CXR dataset (45K pairs) written by professional radiologists for further alignment. For each dataset, we provide the number of cases, release year, label classes and type, label source, and geographical region.
</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<figure id="S0.T2" class="ltx_table">
<div id="S0.T2.3" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:46.6pt;vertical-align:-21.9pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-142.9pt,19.3pt) scale(0.546907974316569,0.546907974316569) ;">
<table id="S0.T2.3.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="S0.T2.3.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
