<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S0.T9.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Extended Data Table 9</span>: </span><span id="S0.T9.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Evaluation of synthetic data for training data augmentation in severity regression.<span id="S0.T9.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Regression models were trained with real data alone and with synthetic data augmentation (1<math id="S0.T9.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> and 2<math id="S0.T9.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math>) for opacity severity scoring on the RALO dataset. Performance is measured using Mean Absolute Error (MAE) and Mean Squared Error (MSE). All results are reported as mean <math id="S0.T9.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>±</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm</annotation></semantics></math> standard deviation over 5 independent runs, with the best performance in each row highlighted in bold. </span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
